aySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-15f6cf183182","stem":"1 Which of the following statements best describes the scapula? UPPER","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It usually overlies the 2nd to 9th ribs."},{"label":"B","text":"The spine continues laterally as the coracoid process."},{"label":"C","text":"The suprascapular notch is found on its spine."},{"label":"D","text":"It provides attachment for both heads of biceps."},{"label":"E","text":"Most fractures involve the body."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4b2aa2bb86c5","stem":"2 Which statement is the best ending for the following sentence? When considering the humerus, it should be noted that the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Upper Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lesser tubercle has three facets."},{"label":"B","text":"Bicipital groove separates the greater and lesser tubercles."},{"label":"C","text":"Surgical neck separates the head from the tubercles."},{"label":"D","text":"Common extensor origin is the medial epicondyle."},{"label":"E","text":"Capitulum articulates with the ulna."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-87abe2bb4dae","stem":"3 Which of the following statements regarding the radius and ulna is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both have a styloid process at the proximal end."},{"label":"B","text":"Both articulate with the humerus at the elbow joint."},{"label":"C","text":"Both articulate with the carpal bones at the wrist joint."},{"label":"D","text":"Direct injury usually produces transverse fractures of both bones in the distal third."},{"label":"E","text":"Fracture is most commonly of the Smith’s type. 1"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"795c5766ee78861ac784ec51dfcbb40a477ba5f4"},{"id":"q-66500c931e83","stem":"4 Which of these statements best describes the carpus? breast?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is markedly concave from side to side anteriorly."},{"label":"B","text":"The most commonly fractured bone is the lunate."},{"label":"C","text":"The scaphoid articulates with the 1st metacarpal."},{"label":"D","text":"Fracture of the hamate may result in damage to the median nerve.UPPER e. The pisiform is usually the first bone to begin ossification. LIMB: 1.5 Which statement most appropriately describes the female"},{"label":"A","text":"It overlies the 3rd to 8th ribs."},{"label":"B","text":"It consists of 2–3 lobules."},{"label":"C","text":"It has suspensory ligaments, which tether the der-QUESTIONS mis to the fascia of the chest wall."},{"label":"D","text":"The retro-mammary space lies deep to pectoralis major."},{"label":"E","text":"The areolar glands are responsible for lactation."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-185d5917408b","stem":"6 Which of these statements best describes the pectoral gir- dle and shoulder?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Shoulder","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The clavicle ossifies in the foetus."},{"label":"B","text":"The clavicle most commonly fractures at the junc- tion of the medial and middle third."},{"label":"C","text":"The subscapularis bursa is separate from the cap- sule of the shoulder joint."},{"label":"D","text":"The capsule of the shoulder joint communicates with the subacromial bursa."},{"label":"E","text":"The short head of biceps lies within the capsule of the shoulder joint."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"9f2761d922e7f1ed1440a8e4788f642334e0583b"},{"id":"q-e33625c9bd41","stem":"7 Which of the following is true of the rotator cuff?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Teres major is one of its four constituent muscles."},{"label":"B","text":"Infraspinatus is innervated by the suprascapular nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"Part of its action is to pull the humeral head superiorly."},{"label":"D","text":"Subscapularis inserts onto the greater tuberosity of the humerus."},{"label":"E","text":"It is deficient anteriorly. 2"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"99e7696940efb84e83d47040e233f1c51ef3bd66"},{"id":"q-a982144edb57","stem":"8 When considering the axilla, which of the following statements is accurate?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pectoralis major and minor contribute to the ante- rior wall."},{"label":"B","text":"The long thoracic nerve runs on the posterior wall."},{"label":"C","text":"Teres minor forms the lower part of the posterior wall."},{"label":"D","text":"The axillary artery lies anterior to the axillary sheath. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"The axillary nerve exits through the triangular space. LIMB:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"a57c3097ddf8580209edbb3f4173d06d13d9dad9"},{"id":"q-b9c75b25d3f2","stem":"9 Which of these sentences best describes the elbow joint? a. The capitulum articulates with the head of the ulna. UPPER","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Head","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The capsule of the joint attaches to the radius."},{"label":"C","text":"The annular ligament is attached to the ulna, but not to the radius."},{"label":"D","text":"The radial nerve is a posterior relation."},{"label":"E","text":"The valgus angle created by the joint is larger in men than in women."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e03cc74ef304","stem":"10 Which statement correctly describes the cubital fossa?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Its borders are entirely muscular."},{"label":"B","text":"A branch of the musculocutaneous nerve is found in its floor."},{"label":"C","text":"The median cubital vein traverses its roof."},{"label":"D","text":"The median nerve lies lateral to the brachial artery within it."},{"label":"E","text":"The radial nerve lies medial to the tendon of biceps within it. 3"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"fd8a6f2f6ff0e3231ad1bcaabc70b509b53ff6af"},{"id":"q-7637fd786bbb","stem":"11 Which of the following accurately describes the anterior compartment of the forearm? by the median nerve.QUESTIONS 1.12 Which of the following best describes the forearm?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The median nerve enters the forearm between the two heads of flexor carpi ulnaris."},{"label":"B","text":"Palmaris longus is present in approximately 15% of arms.UPPER c. Flexor digitorum profundus originates from the common flexor origin. LIMB: d. Flexor pollicis longus is characteristically uni- pennate."},{"label":"E","text":"The superficial flexor muscles are all innervated"},{"label":"A","text":"The median nerve is related anteriorly to flexor digitorum superficialis."},{"label":"B","text":"Pronator quadratus lies deep to the long flexor tendons just proximal to the wrist."},{"label":"C","text":"The ulnar nerve lies superficial to flexor carpi ulnaris."},{"label":"D","text":"Flexor digitorum profundus is partially supplied by the posterior interosseous nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The radial nerve carries motor fibres in the anter- ior compartment of the forearm."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-10d8322935e1","stem":"13 Which of the following statements best describes the structures in the posterior compartment of the forearm?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Brachioradialis is innervated by the posterior interosseous nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"The common extensor origin is the medial epi- condyle of the humerus."},{"label":"C","text":"The posterior interosseous nerve pierces supinator."},{"label":"D","text":"The extensor retinaculum is attached to the radius and the ulna."},{"label":"E","text":"The extensor tendons pass through the extensor retinaculum in the same fascial compartment. 4"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"bc482eea3c351fbb4b66b09cda6ab9e9d21c9573"},{"id":"q-4aeb1ad124ad","stem":"14 Which of these statements about the wrist joint is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Wrist","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a synovial joint between the ulna and the carpal bones."},{"label":"B","text":"The triquetral articulates with the ulna."},{"label":"C","text":"The joint line lies at the level of the styloid pro- cess of the ulna."},{"label":"D","text":"It has palmar, dorsal and collateral ligaments. e. The capsule is continuous with the distal radio- QUESTIONS ulnar joint. LIMB:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"993c0dd20d0dbe4543c783bad4908df98fd92850"},{"id":"q-2f6e8b8b0ec9","stem":"15 Which of the following statements best describes the carpal tunnel? a. The flexor retinaculum is attached to the UPPER trapezoid.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Ophthalmology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The tendons of flexor digitorum superficialis lie with the index and little finger tendons anterior to those of the middle and ring fingers."},{"label":"C","text":"The median nerve lies directly deep to the ten- dons of flexor digitorum superficialis."},{"label":"D","text":"The palmar cutaneous branch of the median nerve lies superficial to the flexor retinaculum."},{"label":"E","text":"The tendon of flexor carpi ulnaris lies within the carpel tunnel."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Ophthalmology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e59674c834f4","stem":"16 The flexor tendons of the forearm run within sheaths in the hand. Which of the following statements best describes these structures?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The fibrous flexor sheaths run from the metacar- pal heads to the proximal phalanges."},{"label":"B","text":"The annular pullies overlie the interphalangeal joints."},{"label":"C","text":"The synovial sheath of the middle finger tendon is continuous with its sheath in the carpal tunnel."},{"label":"D","text":"The cruciform pullies overlie the phalanges."},{"label":"E","text":"The flexor digitorum profundus tendon pierces the flexor digitorum superficialis tendon. 5"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"3bfb8f14e2ef8e56344788bd60b7f070f6af1c49"},{"id":"q-526539f9c1ac","stem":"17 Which statement regarding the anatomical snuffbox is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Abductor pollicis longus and extensor pollicis brevis form the ulnar border."},{"label":"B","text":"The extensor pollicis longus tendon forms the radial border.UPPER c. The floor is formed by the scaphoid and trapezoid."},{"label":"D","text":"The radial artery runs in the floor. LIMB: e. The origin of the basilic vein is found in its roof."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"66a8a3cb54791e9bc5fbba9c58f10df0670533a3"},{"id":"q-a65e8a68544f","stem":"18 Which statement regarding the anatomical spaces of the hand is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Hand","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The thenar space lies lateral to the 3rd metacarpal.QUESTIONS b. The hypothenar space lies lateral to the 5th metacarpal."},{"label":"C","text":"The midpalmar space lies superficial to the pal- mar aponeurosis."},{"label":"D","text":"The pulp spaces lie on the dorsal aspect of the fingers and thumb."},{"label":"E","text":"The web spaces lie between adjacent metacarpal bones."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"aef83fff80b996e48d497e13f44848de26a5b9f0"},{"id":"q-ba5339f4da40","stem":"19 Which of the following best describes the lumbricals?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The lumbricals arise from the tendons of flexor digitorum superficialis."},{"label":"B","text":"There is a lumbrical inserted into the extensor expansion of all five digits."},{"label":"C","text":"The median and radial nerves innervate the lumbricals."},{"label":"D","text":"The action of the lumbricals is to extend the dis- tal interphalangeal joint."},{"label":"E","text":"The action of the lumbricals is to flex the proximal interphalangeal joint. 6"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"7d917775a5364d47619d8b554a467c04043a0b07"},{"id":"q-d8430eb977d9","stem":"20 The following are statements about the interosseous muscles of the hand. Which is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Hand","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The palmar interossei abduct the fingers."},{"label":"B","text":"There are four palmar interossei."},{"label":"C","text":"There are three dorsal interossei."},{"label":"D","text":"The dorsal interossei are bipennate."},{"label":"E","text":"The palmar interossei are all supplied by the median nerve. QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b1d3e39fa3cb69464466b95992189cdd91cb66f6"},{"id":"q-b4ac52e94d57","stem":"21 These statements consider the vasculature and lymph- atic drainage of the breast. Which is true? LIMB","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The main blood supply is derived from branches of the internal mammary artery. b. Venous drainage is predominantly to the internal UPPER mammary vein."},{"label":"C","text":"Lymphatic drainage is divided evenly between the axillary and internal mammary nodes."},{"label":"D","text":"The superficial lymphatics of each breast remain separate in healthy people."},{"label":"E","text":"All the axillary lymphatics drain through the apical axillary nodes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-639ed5a4a248","stem":"22 Which of the following statements best describes the subclavian artery?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is divided into three parts by the scalenus medius muscle."},{"label":"B","text":"The second part gives no constant branch."},{"label":"C","text":"It is crossed posteriorly by the vagus nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"It lies anterior to the subclavian vein."},{"label":"E","text":"It is prone to aneurysmal change in the presence of a cervical rib. 7"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"25157598ba95f143ba6f7bad8a8fa819aef83549"},{"id":"q-3863dfe1f302","stem":"23 Which of the following statements about the axillary artery is accurate?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is divided into three parts by pectoralis major."},{"label":"B","text":"It becomes the brachial artery at the inferior bor- der of teres minor."},{"label":"C","text":"The cords of the brachial plexus are named accord-UPPER ing to their positions relative to the first part."},{"label":"D","text":"The axillary vein lies medial throughout its course. LIMB: e. It gives the suprascapular artery as one of its branches."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"04b02294ccc5e8d4d47de5dad3870ca212126be8"},{"id":"q-dbd93ed9a100","stem":"24 The brachial plexus gives rise to the nerve supply of the upper limb. Which of these statements about itsQUESTIONS branches is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Brachial","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The terminal branch of the medial cord is the ulnar nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"The terminal branch of the posterior cord is the median nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"The axillary nerve is a branch of the lateral cord."},{"label":"D","text":"The radial nerve arises from the medial cord."},{"label":"E","text":"The long thoracic nerve arises from the roots."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["scientific_ambiguity_multiple_plausible_options"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-70db76048f20","stem":"25 Which of these statements about the musculocutaneous nerve is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Brachial Plexus · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Brachial Plexus","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus."},{"label":"B","text":"It pierces brachialis to enter the anterior compart- ment of the arm."},{"label":"C","text":"Brachioradialis is innervated by one of its branches."},{"label":"D","text":"The medial cutaneous nerve of the forearm is its terminal branch."},{"label":"E","text":"It contributes to the innervation of the shoulder joint. 8"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Brachial Plexus · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"911d441d8c3e023abb5c62bb86e01a552e9d90bb"},{"id":"q-71afcedf801b","stem":"26 Select the most appropriate ending for the following sentence. The median nerve","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Upper Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Arises from both the posterior and medial cords of the brachial plexus."},{"label":"B","text":"Passes from the medial to the lateral side of the brachial artery in the arm."},{"label":"C","text":"Gives no muscular branches in the arm."},{"label":"D","text":"Enters the forearm by passing between the two heads of flexor carpi ulnaris. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"Supplies all of flexor digitorum profundus. LIMB:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5aa628927718","stem":"27 Which of these statements best completes the following sentence? The ulnar nerve: a. Has the ulnar artery as a medial relation at the UPPER wrist.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Wrist","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Passes deep to the flexor retinaculum at the wrist."},{"label":"C","text":"Usually innervates the lateral two lumbricals."},{"label":"D","text":"Innervates adductor pollicis."},{"label":"E","text":"Innervates the skin of the lateral (radial) 11⁄2 digits."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-aa2b78b524a9","stem":"28 Which statement considering the relations of nerves to the humerus is the most accurate?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Upper Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The axillary nerve runs around the anatomical neck."},{"label":"B","text":"The median nerve runs in the spiral groove."},{"label":"C","text":"Mid-shaft humeral fractures will usually result in complete paralysis of triceps."},{"label":"D","text":"The ulnar nerve is related to the lateral epicondyle."},{"label":"E","text":"Deltoid may atrophy following shoulder dislocation. 9"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"b1f3f8db345b5c0f761e4650bb4e5cab81a28233"},{"id":"q-0602dde71b29","stem":"29 Consider the dermatomes of the upper limb. Which of the following statements best completes this sentence? The skin over the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Upper Limb","topicOriginal":"Upper Limb","subtopic":"Upper Limb","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Clavicle derives its cutaneous innervation from C4."},{"label":"B","text":"Thumb derives its cutaneous innervation from T1."},{"label":"C","text":"Little finger derives its cutaneous innervationUPPER from C7."},{"label":"D","text":"Posterior surface of the forearm derives its cuta- LIMB: neous innervation from T1."},{"label":"E","text":"Lateral aspect of the upper limb derives its cuta- neous innervation from C8 and T1."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Upper Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-263c7afc0920","stem":"30 Which of the following statements ends this sentence correctly? The spinal nerve root mediating the:QUESTIONS","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Biceps jerk is C5."},{"label":"B","text":"Supinator jerk is C7."},{"label":"C","text":"Triceps jerk is C6."},{"label":"D","text":"Deltoid reflex is C4."},{"label":"E","text":"Pectoral reflex is C5. 10 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c3965b7c8a76","stem":"29 UPPERa. The statement is correct. Explanations","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The hand derives its cutaneous innervation from C6, C7 and C8, with the thumb being innervated by fibres derived from C6. 25"},{"label":"C","text":"The skin overlying the little finger derives its cutaneous innervation from C8."},{"label":"D","text":"The posterior surface of the forearm is innervated by fibres from C6, C7 and C8. The dermatomes are organised in this order from proximal to distal."},{"label":"E","text":"The lateral aspect of the upper limb is supplied by fibres arising from C5 and C6. The medial aspect of the upper limb is innervated by fibres from C8 and T1."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-b09d8e0d0160","stem":"30 a The biceps jerk principally tests the C5 reflex arc, with a contribution from C6. Explanations","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"B","text":"The supinator jerk corresponds primarily to the C6 reflex arc, with a contribution from C5."},{"label":"C","text":"The triceps jerk is principally mediated by C7, with a con- tribution from C8."},{"label":"D","text":"This reflex may be of occasional use, and is elicited by placing the examiner’s index finger across the tip of the shoulder on the deltoid muscle belly, and tapping the fin- ger. It solely tests the reflex arc of spinal cord segment C5."},{"label":"E","text":"The pectoral reflex is elicited by placing the examiner’s index and middle fingers on the lateral border of pectoralis major and tapping them with a tendon hammer. It tests the reflex arc of C7. UPPER LIMB: ANSWERS 26 2 Lower Limb QUESTIONS QUESTIONS LIMB:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f0f4b6ea2450bc4d2e6e664514fd2947d4ca5a8f"},{"id":"q-2ab680b837ff","stem":"1 Which of these statements about the femur is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Lower Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The intertrochanteric line lies on the anterior LOWER aspect of the bone."},{"label":"B","text":"The lateral condyle projects more anteriorly than the medial condyle."},{"label":"C","text":"Gluteus minimus is attached to the lesser trochanter."},{"label":"D","text":"The intertrochanteric crest is the insertion point for the quadratus femoris."},{"label":"E","text":"Gluteus maximus attaches to the gluteal tuberosity."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"887513fe7a9a6902f6eff3677958a819a4f891c4"},{"id":"q-e7100e7ebca0","stem":"2 Which of these statements about the tibia and fibula is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Lower Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The medial tibial condyle is smaller and more cir- cular than the lateral."},{"label":"B","text":"Sartorius, gracilis and semitendinosus insert into the tibia."},{"label":"C","text":"Popliteus arises below the soleal line."},{"label":"D","text":"The common fibular nerve is subcutaneous at the neck of the fibula."},{"label":"E","text":"The fibularis muscles arise from the anterior sur- face of the fibula. 27"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"5dcdaf38c5a00e2c6ddf26347a1a8d90f0beab6b"},{"id":"q-1599783e3eb1","stem":"3 Which statement about the arches of the foot is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Foot","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The medial arch contains the medial cuneiform as one of its bony elements."},{"label":"B","text":"The lateral arch contains the lateral two metatar- sals as bony elements."},{"label":"C","text":"Flexor hallucis longus is important in maintainingLOWER the stability of the lateral arch."},{"label":"D","text":"Fibularis longus helps to maintain the lateral arch.LIMB: e. Fibularis longus helps to maintain the transverse arch."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2c2998ae97639a4455a4abfd87bf28198bdca114"},{"id":"q-ed68d81ab70a","stem":"4 Which of the following best describes the anatomy of the gluteal muscles?QUESTIONS","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gluteus maximus is supplied by the superior glu- teal artery."},{"label":"B","text":"Gluteus maximus inserts into the greater trochanter."},{"label":"C","text":"Gluteus medius is a lateral rotator at the hip joint."},{"label":"D","text":"They all take origin from the ilium."},{"label":"E","text":"Gluteus minimus is innervated by the inferior glu- teal nerve."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8dbde2681737","stem":"5 Which of the following statements incorrectly describes the relations of the hip joint?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Hip","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Rectus femoris is a superior relation."},{"label":"B","text":"Obturator externus is an inferior relation."},{"label":"C","text":"The iliotibial tract is a lateral relation."},{"label":"D","text":"The femoral vein is an anterior relation."},{"label":"E","text":"Pectineus is a lateral relation."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8bcfe3ad776c980b15a78171c13746cb9ded2529"},{"id":"q-cf580c7b3c79","stem":"6 Consider the fascia and compartments of the thigh, Which statement is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Thigh","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The iliotibial tract lies superficial to the fascia lata."},{"label":"B","text":"The iliotibial tract inserts onto the lateral epi- condyle of the femur."},{"label":"C","text":"The femoral vein passes through the fascia lata."},{"label":"D","text":"There are three compartments."},{"label":"E","text":"There are three intermuscular septa in the thigh. 28"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f95318e2c06fd77cba203084ba2aef2b7f94c100"},{"id":"q-13fdcf2530b1","stem":"7 Consider these statements about the anterior compart- ment of the thigh, Which of them is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Thigh","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"All the muscles of the anterior compartment are innervated by the femoral nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"Sartorius flexes both the hip and knee joint."},{"label":"C","text":"The quadriceps tendon inserts directly onto the tibia."},{"label":"D","text":"Quadriceps femoris flexes the hip joint. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"Vastus medialis is of importance in preventing lat- eral dislocation of the patella. LIMB:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4cf8e0faba10aecf01464cc19aecd053d011f132"},{"id":"q-81b103193a58","stem":"8 Which statement best describes the medial compartment of the thigh? a. Adductor magnus, longus and brevis insert onto LOWER the linea aspera.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Thigh","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"All the muscles of the medial compartment are innervated by the obturator nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"All the muscles of the medial compartment take origin from the ischium."},{"label":"D","text":"The obturator nerve is split into anterior and pos- terior divisions by adductor longus."},{"label":"E","text":"All the muscles of the medial compartment insert onto the femur."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0a84c718fc72","stem":"9 Which statement best describes the posterior compart- ment of the thigh?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Thigh","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The common origin for the posterior thigh muscles (hamstrings) is the ischial spine."},{"label":"B","text":"Adductor magnus is a muscle of the posterior compartment."},{"label":"C","text":"All the hamstring muscles are innervated by the obturator nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"Both heads of biceps femoris take origin from the pelvis."},{"label":"E","text":"Most of the skin overlying the posterior aspect of the thigh is innervated by the sciatic nerve. 29"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"9dead154430f140205fe6aef636a3a1d545cb27c"},{"id":"q-75e1b49983ad","stem":"10 Consider the femoral sheath and canal, Which of these statements is not correct? LIMB: 2.11 Which statement correctly describes the femoral triangle?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Femoral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The femoral sheath is continuous with the trans- versalis fascia."},{"label":"B","text":"The sheath contains the femoral nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"The femoral canal lies medial within the sheath."},{"label":"D","text":"The canal is wider in the female.LOWER"},{"label":"E","text":"The canal contains Cloquet’s node."},{"label":"A","text":"Its medial boundary is the lateral border of adductor longus."},{"label":"B","text":"The floor is formed by the fascia lata."},{"label":"C","text":"The femoral vein passes to lie anterior to theQUESTIONS femoral artery at the apex."},{"label":"D","text":"It contains the short saphenous vein."},{"label":"E","text":"It contains the saphenous nerve."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-acac5ec3424f","stem":"12 Which of these statements about the adductor canal is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is the communication between the femoral tri- angle and popliteal fossa."},{"label":"B","text":"It is bordered posteriorly by adductor longus and magnus."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains the nerve to vastus medialis."},{"label":"D","text":"The saphenous nerve exits the canal medially."},{"label":"E","text":"The femoral artery exits through a hiatus in adductor longus. 30"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"504135c8e5f6ae0ff4a9d5bdd9dc6dd81a1cec23"},{"id":"q-383d08e76e86","stem":"13 Which statement does not correctly describe the liga- ments of the knee joint?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Knee","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The medial meniscus is larger than the lateral meniscus."},{"label":"B","text":"The lateral meniscus is attached to the lateral col- lateral ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The transverse ligament of the knee attaches to both menisci. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"D","text":"The anterior cruciate ligament prevents hyper- extension of the knee. LIMB: e. The posterior cruciate ligament inserts onto the medial femoral condyle."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4f32d71a43bed9895feb4ef0799ebf856f8632b5"},{"id":"q-f0e9f5a6c807","stem":"14 Which of the following statements correctly describes LOWER the capsule of the knee joint?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Knee","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is thickest anteriorly."},{"label":"B","text":"The suprapatellar bursa communicates with the knee joint."},{"label":"C","text":"Both the cruciate ligaments lie within the syn- ovial cavity."},{"label":"D","text":"The infrapatellar fat pad contains the subcutane- ous infrapatellar bursa."},{"label":"E","text":"The posterior meniscofemoral ligament arises from the medial meniscus."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7f9c760973c4","stem":"15 Which statement about the popliteal fossa is not true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is bounded superolaterally by biceps femoris."},{"label":"B","text":"Contains the popliteal artery as the deepest structure."},{"label":"C","text":"Usually contains the bifurcation of the sciatic nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"Contains the long saphenous vein in its roof."},{"label":"E","text":"Contains the formation of the sural nerve. 31"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"401108740a2047ebfa9e532899d7df3db4297eee"},{"id":"q-f9b856853ca9","stem":"16 Which statement correctly describes the anterior com- partment of the leg?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Leg","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is separated from the posterior compartment by the anterior intermuscular septum."},{"label":"B","text":"All the muscles of the compartment are innerv- ated by the deep peroneal nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"The anterior tibial artery arises in the anteriorLOWER compartment."},{"label":"D","text":"It contains extensor digitorum brevis.LIMB: e. Tibialis anterior assists in eversion of the foot."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3ff23b019086b52696c3ac3fccc4eef26e745cba"},{"id":"q-2ce1665e3bb9","stem":"17 Consider the lateral compartment of the leg. Which statement is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Leg","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"All the muscles of the lateral compartment areQUESTIONS innervated by the superficial peroneal nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"It contains the peroneal artery."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains peroneus longus, brevis and tertius."},{"label":"D","text":"The peroneus longus tendon grooves the lateral malleolus."},{"label":"E","text":"The muscles of the lateral compartment princi- pally invert the foot."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d76d5d5cf20b9e9eb0333d033c7b5d839607355d"},{"id":"q-f6c4b0ecdb0b","stem":"18 Which statement regarding the tendons of the muscles of the lateral compartment of the leg is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Leg","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The peroneus longus tendon runs posterior to that of peroneus brevis at the lateral malleolus."},{"label":"B","text":"Both tendons pass under the superior and infer- ior peroneal retinaculae."},{"label":"C","text":"They share a common synovial sheath as they pass under both retinaculae."},{"label":"D","text":"The tendons are separated by the peroneal trochlea."},{"label":"E","text":"The peroneus longus tendon passes deep to the long plantar ligament. 32"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"00b0c8ee161333654a50244a9bf5a2aa448e46ef"},{"id":"q-e7317203fdfa","stem":"19 Which of the following does not correctly describe the posterior compartment of the leg?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Leg","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The muscles are separated into deep and superfi- cial groups by the posterior intermuscular septum."},{"label":"B","text":"All of the muscles are innervated by the tibial nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains both the anterior and posterior tibial arteries. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"D","text":"Flexor hallucis longus takes origin from the fib- ula, lateral to flexor digitorum longus. LIMB: e. Popliteus unlocks the knee by laterally rotating the femur."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5ca0f1618a01c4b62df198fcc8f24ae2a3966603"},{"id":"q-2475960bc088","stem":"20 Which statement, regarding the arterial anastomosis LOWER around the hip joint is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Hip","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The circumflex femoral arteries usually arise from the profunda femoris."},{"label":"B","text":"The artery to the head of the femur is a branch of the femoral artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The artery to the head of the femur enters with the ligamentum teres."},{"label":"D","text":"The hip joint is supplied by retinacular branches."},{"label":"E","text":"Avascular necrosis is common in fractures of the femoral neck."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-40e48665f3fb","stem":"21 Which statement best describes the common femoral artery?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Femoral","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Commences at the midpoint of the inguinal ligament."},{"label":"B","text":"Gives the profunda femoris branch within the femoral sheath."},{"label":"C","text":"Lies between the saphenous nerve and femoral vein at all levels of the thigh."},{"label":"D","text":"Lies over pectineus as it passes under the inguinal ligament."},{"label":"E","text":"Becomes the popliteal artery as it leaves the fem- oral triangle. 33"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"c6253be3138c4d7510ecc3edd30eb2907b303be3"},{"id":"q-e6d7c8b97924","stem":"22 Which of the following associations of lower limb move- ments and root values is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb","topicOriginal":"Lower Limb","subtopic":"Lower Limb","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hip flexion L3, L4"},{"label":"B","text":"Knee flexion L5, S1"},{"label":"C","text":"Ankle dorsiflexion L4, L5"},{"label":"D","text":"Inversion L4"},{"label":"E","text":"Eversion L5, S1LOWER LIMB: QUESTIONS 34 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"b38a8824e19f7620552e3a4d307476da310cf17e"},{"id":"q-91ca2321521d","stem":"1 Which of the following statements about the surface anatomy of the chest is correct? THORAX","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Face","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The manubrium overlies the aortic arch at the level of T4–T5."},{"label":"B","text":"The body of the sternum overlies the heart at the level of T5–T8."},{"label":"C","text":"The most prominent vertebral spinous process encountered when palpating the spine is that of C6."},{"label":"D","text":"The manubriosternal joint is at the level of the junction of T3 and T4."},{"label":"E","text":"The xiphisternal joint is at the level of T8."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ca65f14637d8","stem":"2 Consider the surface markings of the pleura, which of the following is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Face","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The right and left pleura come into contact in the midline at the level of the jugular notch (supraster- nal notch)."},{"label":"B","text":"The apex of the pleura is approximately level with the clavicle."},{"label":"C","text":"The right pleura passes across the 10th rib in the anterior axillary line."},{"label":"D","text":"The left pleura arches laterally at the level of the 4th costal cartilage."},{"label":"E","text":"The pleura terminates above the level of the 12th rib. 49"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f269a945755057431d72e78433014808db89a8bc"},{"id":"q-008d865112bb","stem":"3 Which statement about the ribs is accurate?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The head of a typical rib articulates with the trans- verse costal facet of its own vertebra."},{"label":"B","text":"The 8th, 9th and 10th ribs are false ribs."},{"label":"C","text":"The 1st rib has the subclavian artery as an inferior relation."},{"label":"D","text":"The costotransverse ligaments pass from the trans- verse process of the vertebra to the head of the rib.THORAX:"},{"label":"E","text":"The intercostal neurovascular bundle has the inter- costal vein as the most inferior structure."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6ba52e1c5d70dc3d565b7960743dd9b08828f58f"},{"id":"q-f22cc0bcffe0","stem":"4 Which of the following statements correctly describes the arterial supply of the body wall?QUESTIONS","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The internal thoracic artery supplies the anterior body wall as far down as the umbilicus."},{"label":"B","text":"The first nine anterior intercostal arteries are direct branches of the internal thoracic artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The posterior intercostal arteries are all branches of the thoracic aorta."},{"label":"D","text":"The lower anterior abdominal wall is supplied by a branch of the internal iliac artery."},{"label":"E","text":"The intercostal veins lie directly superior to the intercostal nerves."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-865d0ae74f56","stem":"5 Which statement regarding the internal thoracic artery is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is a branch of the aorta."},{"label":"B","text":"It arises from the brachiocephalic artery on the right side."},{"label":"C","text":"It lies between the external and internal intercos- tal muscles."},{"label":"D","text":"It contributes to the blood supply of the breast."},{"label":"E","text":"The pericardiophrenic artery is a terminal branch. 50"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"292aaa93de3d7b13edac44867b26d75fa0ab79d2"},{"id":"q-3aa7bd8bcf03","stem":"6 Which of the following statements best describes the lungs?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Lung","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both main bronchi enter the roots of their respect- ive lungs at the level of T6."},{"label":"B","text":"The left main bronchus gives its upper lobe bron- chus before joining the lung."},{"label":"C","text":"The blood supply of the lung is derived from the pulmonary arteries."},{"label":"D","text":"The left lung has a lingular segment. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"Blood from the lungs drains directly into the bra- chiocephalic trunks."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"19cc1331621f0a9fd3e2db075bbea13747e7f8e6"},{"id":"q-84c25c53cfbc","stem":"7 Which of the following structures does not enter the THORAX: hilum of the left lung?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The left upper lobe bronchus."},{"label":"B","text":"The left pulmonary artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The bronchial artery."},{"label":"D","text":"Branches of the pulmonary plexus."},{"label":"E","text":"Lymphatics which drain into the bronchopulmo- nary lymph nodes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ffc5969901da","stem":"8 Which of the following statements regarding the divisions of the mediastinum is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Mediastin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The superior mediastinum lies above the level of the T3/T4 intervertebral disc."},{"label":"B","text":"The inferior mediastinum is conventionally divided into three parts."},{"label":"C","text":"The descending thoracic aorta is entirely in the middle mediastinum."},{"label":"D","text":"The pericardial sac and its contents form the anter- ior mediastinum."},{"label":"E","text":"The phrenic nerves run in the anterior compartment. 51"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f1fe7d70b429bdbc066b8fcfd2d636e56989ae4e"},{"id":"q-e016afd821a7","stem":"9 Which of these statements regarding the superior media- stinum is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The right brachiocephalic vein is shorter than the left."},{"label":"B","text":"The vagus nerve enters the thorax posterior to the subclavian artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The ligamentum arteriosum usually passes from the left pulmonary artery to the ascending aorta.THORAX:"},{"label":"D","text":"The thoracic duct passes across the oesophagus within the superior mediastinum."},{"label":"E","text":"The left phrenic nerve passes medial to the aortic arch.QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"87d9a1a5a98ec74f8ad1f9d283846708d3d0345f"},{"id":"q-10e137a06045","stem":"10 Which of the following statements regarding the trachea is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It commences at the level of C8."},{"label":"B","text":"It is in contact with the left vagus nerve in the thorax."},{"label":"C","text":"It has a blood supply from the superior thyroid arteries."},{"label":"D","text":"It is lined by mucus secreting cells."},{"label":"E","text":"It bifurcates at the level of the T2/T3 interverte- bral disc."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"c33a735dc8ff12ed4fce0cb6cfa1197c6bfa8fc0"},{"id":"q-cf38ea8bfb48","stem":"11 Which of the following statements about the oesopha- gus is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is crossed anteriorly by the left main bronchus."},{"label":"B","text":"Passes through the diaphragm with the left phrenic nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"Has a blood supply from the superior thyroid artery."},{"label":"D","text":"Has a venous drainage into the right gastric vein."},{"label":"E","text":"Has smooth muscle in the lower 2/3 of its wall. 52"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"4a87e9a93f3d17a0e9da730991c56bbf9b384c30"},{"id":"q-d3ba0fdb081e","stem":"12 Which statement regarding the superior vena cava is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is formed by the union of the right and left subclavian veins."},{"label":"B","text":"The azygos vein drains into its posterior aspect."},{"label":"C","text":"It drains blood from all structures superior to the diaphragm."},{"label":"D","text":"It forms the posterior boundary of the oblique pericardial sinus. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"Has a rudimentary valve at its opening into the right atrium."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"20a54525c5572824ed24ad016b397247f03aa2a0"},{"id":"q-44faca84f9c3","stem":"13 Which of the following statements does not correctly THORAX: describe the pericardium?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The oblique sinus is bounded by the pulmonary veins and the pulmonary arteries."},{"label":"B","text":"The transverse sinus lies between the superior vena cava and left atrium posteriorly, and the arch of aorta and pulmonary trunk anteriorly."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains the entire ascending aorta."},{"label":"D","text":"It is attached to the central tendon of the diaphragm."},{"label":"E","text":"The phrenic nerves are directly related to its lat- eral surface on both sides."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f6b302a62a93","stem":"14 Which of these statements does not correctly describe the phrenic nerve?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It innervates the mediastinal pleura."},{"label":"B","text":"It innervates the diaphragm from its superior sur- face downwards."},{"label":"C","text":"It passes anterior to the hilum of the lung on the left."},{"label":"D","text":"It lies lateral to the superior vena cava on the right."},{"label":"E","text":"It has the subclavian artery on its medial side on the left. 53"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"977cd8a3cb77f947cea3dea755165f80afa1574f"},{"id":"q-3982207028cc","stem":"15 Consider these statements about the heart, which one is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The right lateral border is formed entirely by the right atrium."},{"label":"B","text":"The left atrium is visible when the anterior sur- face of the heart is viewed."},{"label":"C","text":"The inferior surface is formed by the left and right ventricles, together with the right atrium.THORAX:"},{"label":"D","text":"The base of the heart is directly related to the surface of the diaphragm."},{"label":"E","text":"The pulmonary trunk arises anterior to the aorta."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"7e90ef18d974d1f4dff4ae762782321aa0dc949a"},{"id":"q-7ed15af42bc5","stem":"16 Which statement about the right atrium is incorrect?QUESTIONS","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Heart and Coronary Vessels · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Heart and Coronary Vessels","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The crista terminalis separates the smooth walled part from the rough walled part."},{"label":"B","text":"The opening of the inferior vena cava into the right atrium is valveless."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains the embryological remnant of the foramen ovale."},{"label":"D","text":"It receives the coronary sinus."},{"label":"E","text":"The smooth walled part is derived from the sinus venosus of the primitive heart tube."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Heart and Coronary Vessels · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-52c84094ad32","stem":"17 Which statement about the left ventricle is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy","topicOriginal":"Neuroanatomy","subtopic":"Ventricle","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The mitral valve is tricuspid."},{"label":"B","text":"The papillary muscles and chordae tendinae anchor the aortic valve."},{"label":"C","text":"It lies posterior to the right ventricle."},{"label":"D","text":"Its wall has a smooth and a rough portion."},{"label":"E","text":"The aortic valve is bicuspid. 54"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2521d4dfe28a693c825335ac5e2270ec1fb9aafc"},{"id":"q-6292e7b7d667","stem":"18 Which statement about the conducting system of the heart is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The sinoatrial node lies in the crista terminalis, next to the entrance of the inferior vena cava."},{"label":"B","text":"The atrioventricular node lies next to the open- ing of the coronary sinus."},{"label":"C","text":"The bundle of His divides in the membranous part of the interventricular septum."},{"label":"D","text":"The right bundle branch has anterior and pos- QUESTIONS terior divisions."},{"label":"E","text":"The sinoatrial node is supplied by the right coro- nary artery in 40% of cases. THORAX:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5dfe6057ca3bbc71328b7c73af36b73271bffaf9"},{"id":"q-38117c6332d2","stem":"19 Which statement about the valves of the heart is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both the pulmonary and aortic valves are bicuspid."},{"label":"B","text":"The 1st heart sound corresponds to closure of the aortic and pulmonary valves."},{"label":"C","text":"Closure of the aortic valve is best heard in the left 2nd intercostal space."},{"label":"D","text":"The chorda tendinae tether the atrioventricular valves to pectinate muscle directly."},{"label":"E","text":"The chorda tendinae prevent eversion of the atrio- ventricular valves."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ccd019d8546cfe0a3f30999ed2aa98fa2fbc252d"},{"id":"q-c7eca2c5a0e5","stem":"20 Which statement about the right coronary artery is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Supplies the atrioventricular node in 90% of cases."},{"label":"B","text":"Usually gives off the posterior interventricular artery."},{"label":"C","text":"Contributes to the posterior interventricular artery in a co-dominant circulation."},{"label":"D","text":"Anastomoses with the circumflex branch of the left coronary artery."},{"label":"E","text":"Arises from the right posterior aortic sinus. 55"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"7ad34d860ca2eba56e3dd8d89ef820e985622a79"},{"id":"q-d72edbb37464","stem":"21 Which statement regarding the left coronary artery is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is usually shorter than the right coronary artery."},{"label":"B","text":"Has an intermediate branch in 1/3 of cases."},{"label":"C","text":"Supplies the sinoatrial node in 40% of cases."},{"label":"D","text":"Gives off the posterior interventricular artery in a left dominant circulation."},{"label":"E","text":"Passes posterior to the left auricle.THORAX:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b0ed806221e8d2e2cdda53b7aa63cd3e8d35fc4f"},{"id":"q-c6aaa84f1f21","stem":"22 Which statement incorrectly describes the venous drain- age of the heart?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Venae cordis minimae drain into all four chambers."},{"label":"B","text":"The anterior cardiac veins drain into the rightQUESTIONS atrium."},{"label":"C","text":"The coronary sinus lies in the posterior interven- tricular groove."},{"label":"D","text":"The middle cardiac vein is a tributary of the cor- onary sinus."},{"label":"E","text":"The small cardiac vein is a tributary of the cor- onary sinus."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"978b6de72ffa18d6a8962a3398a113a1f4107bc0"},{"id":"q-a524af460bc9","stem":"23 Which statement about the primitive aortic arches is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The first arches persist."},{"label":"B","text":"The second arches become the carotids."},{"label":"C","text":"The third arches disappear."},{"label":"D","text":"The fourth arch links up with the descending aorta on the left side."},{"label":"E","text":"The fifth arches become the pulmonary arteries. 56"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"e011a71f8fb884f4a6cea9284070e3a454247ad7"},{"id":"q-b37470e31d76","stem":"24 Which statement regarding the foetal circulation is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The septum secundum lies to the left of the sep- tum primum."},{"label":"B","text":"The ductus arteriosus closes at birth."},{"label":"C","text":"The foramen ovale is a defect in the septum primum."},{"label":"D","text":"The ligamentum teres is the embryological rem- nant of the right umbilical vein. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"The umbilical arteries are derived from branches of the external iliac arteries."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"f676ed3a8ee201fbcb213b317a522a1167d98618"},{"id":"q-999bfd08111c","stem":"25 Which statement concerning the azygos system is THORAX: incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Thorax","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It comprises veins on either side of the thoracic spine."},{"label":"B","text":"The azygos vein passes through the diaphragm with the aorta."},{"label":"C","text":"The hemiazygos vein passes through the dia- phragm with the aorta."},{"label":"D","text":"The anterior intercostal veins are tributaries of the hemiazygos vein."},{"label":"E","text":"The hemiazygos and accessory hemiazygos veins drain into the azygos vein."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b1c65b1df915","stem":"26 Which of the following statements does not correctly describe the thoracic duct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It originates from the cisterna chyli."},{"label":"B","text":"It passes through the diaphragm with the aorta."},{"label":"C","text":"It drains all the body tissue below the diaphragm."},{"label":"D","text":"It usually drains the entire left side of the body."},{"label":"E","text":"It empties into the left subclavian artery. 57"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"b3ede45511ad03c1bb661c11bd0d7ae40bd4971d"},{"id":"q-4320955f49d1","stem":"27 Which of these statements about the descending aorta is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The descending aorta forms at the level of T6."},{"label":"B","text":"The aortic hiatus is at the level of T10."},{"label":"C","text":"The aorta usually gives rise to the majority of the posterior intercostal arteries."},{"label":"D","text":"Isolated coarctation usually occurs at the level of the hiatus.THORAX:"},{"label":"E","text":"Gives rise to a pair of subcostal arteries below the diaphragm."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e62249bc9308ad341406935697e30d0de961188c"},{"id":"q-b070cd3dd608","stem":"28 Which of the following statements regarding the thor- acic sympathetic chain is incorrect?QUESTIONS","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It crosses the neck of the 1st rib."},{"label":"B","text":"It exits the thorax by passing beneath the lateral arcuate ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"It gives off the splanchnic nerves."},{"label":"D","text":"It gives post-ganglionic fibres to the thoracic viscera."},{"label":"E","text":"The first thoracic ganglion may be involved in the formation of the stellate ganglion."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3b658228116e","stem":"29 Which statement correctly describes the left vagus nerve?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is the most anterior structure in the carotid sheath."},{"label":"B","text":"It gives a recurrent laryngeal branch which hooks around the left subclavian artery."},{"label":"C","text":"It passes posterior to the aortic arch."},{"label":"D","text":"It passes anterior to the root of the left lung."},{"label":"E","text":"Its fibres pass to the oesophagus to form the oesophageal plexus. 58"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"70e1c8c2a41daa5299003dc5f01dfd270e09dd95"},{"id":"q-119d9a5c6ec0","stem":"30 Which of the following statements best describes the diaphragm?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thorax","topicOriginal":"Thorax","subtopic":"Diaphragm","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is attached to the xiphoid."},{"label":"B","text":"It is attached to the upper three lumbar vertebrae on the left."},{"label":"C","text":"The oesophagus passes through it at the level of T8."},{"label":"D","text":"The left phrenic nerve pierces the diaphragm with the inferior vena cava. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"A congenital Bochdalek hernia occurs anteriorly. THORAX: 59 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thorax","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"0c597de437241955afc2c52cdcc4c03f3d9d1783"},{"id":"q-6fe84799a2c6","stem":"1 Which statement best describes the planes of the abdomen? ABDOMEN","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Abdomen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The transpyloric plane lies halfway between the xiphoid and the symphysis pubis."},{"label":"B","text":"The transpyloric plane passes through the hilar of the kidneys."},{"label":"C","text":"The subcostal plane is at the level of the body of L2."},{"label":"D","text":"The iliac crests lie at the level of L5."},{"label":"E","text":"The umbilicus usually lies at the level of the L4/L5 disc."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c324c4edd135","stem":"2 Which statement about the regions of the abdomen is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Abdomen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The epigastrium lies medial to the mid-clavicular line and above the transpyloric plane."},{"label":"B","text":"The suprapubic region lies between the mid- clavicular lines, the transpyloric plane and the intertubercular line."},{"label":"C","text":"The iliac fossa lies lateral to the mid-clavicular line and above the intertubercular line."},{"label":"D","text":"The hypochondrium lies below the transpyloric plane and medial to the mid-clavicular line."},{"label":"E","text":"The mid-clavicular line crosses the midpoint of the inguinal ligament. 75"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"3ed84d7404598186e205f23bb0bf9d1ce851000d"},{"id":"q-e656f2edc715","stem":"3 Which statement correctly describes the abdominal wall?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The superficial fascia of the abdominal wall con- tains Camper’s fascia."},{"label":"B","text":"The deep fascia of the abdominal wall is known as Scarpa’s fascia."},{"label":"C","text":"Scarpa’s fascia adheres to the superficial fascia of the thigh."},{"label":"D","text":"The umbilicus receives sensory fibres from T8.ABDOMEN: e. The groin is innervated by T12."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"26fe9569fa5cdd33b85cb5ddc54682cdce3f0f4a"},{"id":"q-2202c1d85671","stem":"4 Which statement about the rectus abdominis is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It has the transversalis fascia posteriorly through- out its length.QUESTIONS b. It has three tendinous intersections which are vis- ible posteriorly."},{"label":"C","text":"It has the aponeuroses of the three oblique abdom- inal muscles anterior to it below the arcuate line."},{"label":"D","text":"The lower free border of the anterior rectus sheath is called the arcuate line."},{"label":"E","text":"The linea alba is a highly vascular structure."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"03deb9ea2b52eddbecf0f5ddb5a6003e063b62c5"},{"id":"q-cadd59a09d20","stem":"5 Which statement about the oblique abdominal muscles is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The fibres of external oblique pass antero-inferiorly."},{"label":"B","text":"The lower fibres of internal oblique form the inguinal ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The external oblique arises from the lower eight ribs."},{"label":"D","text":"Internal oblique arises from the lumbar fascia."},{"label":"E","text":"The internal oblique has a free lower border. 76"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"3c9cb8c5deb6e8ee3219cd45ec44ea2f4e7db4c3"},{"id":"q-d7c5bfd6c6cd","stem":"6 Which statement best completes this sentence? The inguinal canal","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has a deep ring, which is a defect in the transver- sus abdominis muscle."},{"label":"B","text":"Is bounded posteriorly by the inguinal ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"Has the internal oblique as part of its posterior wall throughout."},{"label":"D","text":"Has the conjoint tendon superiorly. e. Transmits the ilioinguinal nerve, which enters the QUESTIONS canal through the deep ring."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-75aced717554","stem":"7 Which of the following statements about the peritoneum is correct? ABDOMEN: a. The median umbilical fold contains the obliterated remnant of the umbilical artery.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Peritone","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The greater omentum consists of four layers of peritoneum."},{"label":"C","text":"The gastrosplenic ligament contains the splenic vessels."},{"label":"D","text":"The lienorenal ligament contains the short gastric vessels."},{"label":"E","text":"The lesser omentum connects the liver to the transverse colon."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2114597c4dcb","stem":"8 Which statement about the lesser sac is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is connected to the greater sac via the epiploic foramen."},{"label":"B","text":"The stomach is related anteriorly."},{"label":"C","text":"The pancreas is a posterior relation."},{"label":"D","text":"The greater omentum is an anterior relation."},{"label":"E","text":"The right border is formed by the lienorenal and gastrosplenic ligaments. 77"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"93fc4cf62223ce86a33969a2c2b8e74221a8b6b3"},{"id":"q-6f803bfbcecf","stem":"9 Which statement about the borders of the epiploic foramen is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The second part of the duodenum forms the infer- ior border."},{"label":"B","text":"The quadrate process of the liver forms the super- ior border."},{"label":"C","text":"The hepatic vein forms the posterior border."},{"label":"D","text":"The free edge of the greater omentum forms theABDOMEN: anterior border."},{"label":"E","text":"The common bile duct is contained within the anterior border."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_provisional_reasoning","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d62c967f345ea524ab421020225512e6725b3b42"},{"id":"q-d362f98e7e97","stem":"10 Which of the following statements regarding peritonealQUESTIONS compartments is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Peritone","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The infracolic compartment lies below the lesser omentum."},{"label":"B","text":"The right and left subphrenic spaces are separated by the coronary ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The right subhepatic space lies between the right lobe of the liver and the right kidney."},{"label":"D","text":"The left subhepatic space is also known as the hepatorenal pouch."},{"label":"E","text":"The right paracolic gutter lies medial to the colon."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-327619f241fd","stem":"11 Which of these statements about the coeliac trunk is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It supplies the foregut and its derivatives."},{"label":"B","text":"It leaves the aorta at the level of L1."},{"label":"C","text":"It gives a left gastric branch that supplies the oesophagus."},{"label":"D","text":"It gives a splenic branch."},{"label":"E","text":"It gives rise to the gastroduodenal artery via its hepatic branch. 78"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"57696de83f393eb81ce6a12816c638ac7585a35a"},{"id":"q-98a98ed9edea","stem":"12 Which statement best describes the blood supply of the stomach? the alimentary tract?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Stomach","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is derived entirely from the superior mesenteric artery."},{"label":"B","text":"The gastroepiploic arteries supply the lesser curvature."},{"label":"C","text":"The right gastric artery is a direct branch of the coeliac axis. d. The left gastroepiploic artery arises directly from QUESTIONS the coeliac trunk."},{"label":"E","text":"The short gastric arteries arise from the splenic artery. ABDOMEN:4.13 Which statement best describes the venous drainage of"},{"label":"A","text":"All blood drains into the portal system."},{"label":"B","text":"The portal vein is formed from the union of the inferior mesenteric and splenic veins."},{"label":"C","text":"The superior mesenteric vein crosses the uncinate process of the pancreas."},{"label":"D","text":"The inferior mesenteric vein passes behind the left renal vein."},{"label":"E","text":"The prepyloric vein is variable in position."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-51b57411229e","stem":"14 Which statement best completes this sentence? The superior mesenteric artery","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Supplies the gut from the pylorus to the terminal ileum."},{"label":"B","text":"Arises from the aorta at the level of L1."},{"label":"C","text":"Runs in front of the body of the pancreas."},{"label":"D","text":"Crosses the second part of the duodenum."},{"label":"E","text":"Supplies the appendix via its right colic branch. 79"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-01a43a6569e1","stem":"15 Which statement best describes the inferior mesenteric artery?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It arises from the aorta at the level of the transpy- loric plane."},{"label":"B","text":"It supplies the mucus membrane of the gut as far as the mid-rectum."},{"label":"C","text":"It gives off a left colic branch."},{"label":"D","text":"It crosses the pelvic brim at the point of bifurca-ABDOMEN: tion of the right common iliac vessels."},{"label":"E","text":"It anastomoses with the superior mesenteric artery via its sigmoid branch."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1d861e6f0deb6254d3f7891bcab8207cc063b8a1"},{"id":"q-f3927ebc54a1","stem":"16 Which statement best describes the lymphatics of theQUESTIONS gastrointestinal tract?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Intestin","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They generally follow routes which are distinct from those taken by the venous drainage of the bowel."},{"label":"B","text":"Peyer’s patches are found on the mesenteric sur- face of the large bowel."},{"label":"C","text":"Lymphoid follicles become less numerous in the distal part of the gut."},{"label":"D","text":"Preaortic nodes lie at the origins of major blood vessels."},{"label":"E","text":"Lymph from the alimentary tract eventually passes into the portal system of veins."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-31db68f121b1","stem":"17 Which statement best describes the stomach?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Stomach","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lymph from the superior 2/3 of the stomach drains into the suprapancreatic nodes."},{"label":"B","text":"All lymph from the stomach drains through the coeliac nodes."},{"label":"C","text":"The gastric branches of the vagi are given of in the greater curve."},{"label":"D","text":"The lower oesophageal sphinchter is supplied by the nerves of Latarjet."},{"label":"E","text":"The antral part of the stomach secretes an acid solution. 80"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"bd1fc9272848c0710119fbb3f287b9c629562a70"},{"id":"q-dcd94b143aaa","stem":"18 Which of the following statements about the duodenum is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The second part overlies the right kidney."},{"label":"B","text":"The transverse mesocolon attaches over the second part."},{"label":"C","text":"The ampulla of Vater lies in the third part."},{"label":"D","text":"The inferior vena cava and aorta lie directly behind the third part. e. The gall bladder overlies the first part. QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5ccf5594de64547808e5677f31b009b6540b44c6"},{"id":"q-802622074262","stem":"19 Which statement regarding the jejunum and ileum is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ileum has thicker walls than the jejunum. ABDOMEN: b. The proximal small intestine is of greater diam- eter than the distal."},{"label":"C","text":"The mesentery of the small intestine is thicker distally."},{"label":"D","text":"The jejunum lies mainly in the umbilical region."},{"label":"E","text":"The mesenteric vessels form more numerous arcades in the ileum."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen and GI Anatomy · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"67dca166b135426c15d8bf74d40dd323576844bd"},{"id":"q-b03879b69da7","stem":"20 Which of these statements regarding Meckel’s diverticu- lum is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is found in about 4% of the population."},{"label":"B","text":"Is always found on the antimesenteric border of the ileum."},{"label":"C","text":"Is usually about 2 cm in length."},{"label":"D","text":"Is usually located about 20 cm from the ileocaecal junction."},{"label":"E","text":"Is usually attached to the umbilicus. 81"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"c422e9d649ad446ddb92d68e31628ff3088b1f2f"},{"id":"q-dbbe5da52b56","stem":"21 Which statement about the appendix is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The taenia coli converge on the base of the appendix."},{"label":"B","text":"The mesoappendix contains the appendicular vessels in its free edge."},{"label":"C","text":"The ileocaecal fold connects the appendix to the ileum."},{"label":"D","text":"The appendix always lies behind the ileum.ABDOMEN: e. The appendix opens into the posteromedial part of the caecum."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"46176611c6924cf4d6fd19ea02191a168a017588"},{"id":"q-4492e18f157e","stem":"22 Which of the following statements best describes the colon?QUESTIONS a. The majority is derived from the primitive hindgut.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"B","text":"It is usually invested with peritoneum on all sides."},{"label":"C","text":"The hepatic flexure is related directly to the liver and right kidney."},{"label":"D","text":"The ascending and descending colon are always retroperitoneal."},{"label":"E","text":"The appendices epiploicae are composed of lymph- oid tissue."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3710fe5ce01c","stem":"23 Which statement most correctly describes the large bowel?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The taenia coli are longer than the colon."},{"label":"B","text":"The descending colon is the longest part."},{"label":"C","text":"The sigmoid colon has a mesentery."},{"label":"D","text":"The parasympathetic supply is entirely derived from the vagus nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The marginal artery lies within the bowel wall. 82"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"86ca1ffdbc1e3c96cfa7f0646cc387864a7bd03a"},{"id":"q-f14afe159825","stem":"24 Which statement about the liver is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Liver","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The gall bladder lies directly anterior to the fis- sure for the ligamentum venosum."},{"label":"B","text":"The ligamentum teres contains the falciform ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The caudate lobe lies anterior to the quadrate lobe."},{"label":"D","text":"The liver is closely related to the abdominal oesophagus. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"The functional lobes of the liver are demarcated by a line drawn between the attachment of the falciform ligament and the fissure for the liga- mentum venosum. ABDOMEN:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1bf2acf9315f30e7296995baf4e1cac2612c5eed"},{"id":"q-648a7edf6ff5","stem":"25 Which statement best completes this sentence? The porta hepatis contains","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The hepatic artery on the left side."},{"label":"B","text":"The common hepatic duct anteriorly."},{"label":"C","text":"The portal vein anteriorly."},{"label":"D","text":"Parasympathetic fibres from the vagus."},{"label":"E","text":"Sympathetic fibres from the hypogastric plexus."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bce2035b4b6c","stem":"26 When considering porto-systemic anastomosis, which of the following statements is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The portal vein is formed by the union of the superior and inferior mesenteric veins."},{"label":"B","text":"There is an anastomosis between the middle and inferior rectal veins."},{"label":"C","text":"There is an anastomosis between the azygos sys- tem and right gastric veins."},{"label":"D","text":"There is a direct anastomosis between the para- umbilical and common iliac veins."},{"label":"E","text":"There is an anastomosis between the colic and retroperitoneal veins. 83"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"62cc8f051f0eb1aaf7d7abe499f64a6d434990c2"},{"id":"q-8b69208e1397","stem":"27 Which statement concerning the peritoneal reflections on the liver is not correct? tem is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Peritone","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The bare area lies between the left and right tri- angular ligaments."},{"label":"B","text":"The coronary ligament is continuous with the fal- ciform ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The inferior vena cava forms a border of the bare area.ABDOMEN: d. The lesser omentum is reflected around the struc- tures of the porta hepatis."},{"label":"E","text":"The bare area is in contact with the right supra- renal gland.QUESTIONS 4.28 Which of the following statements about the biliary sys-"},{"label":"A","text":"The pancreatic duct drains into the hepatic duct."},{"label":"B","text":"The common hepatic duct is formed by the union of the common bile and cystic ducts."},{"label":"C","text":"Callot’s triangle is formed by the hepatic duct, cystic duct and the cystic artery."},{"label":"D","text":"The common bile duct runs behind the first part of the duodenum."},{"label":"E","text":"The common bile duct runs between the head of the pancreas and the third part of the duodenum."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b2511763e73b","stem":"29 Which statement concerning the relations of the kid- neys is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The diaphragm is directly related to the superior pole of both kidneys."},{"label":"B","text":"The left kidney is related to the duodenum."},{"label":"C","text":"The kidneys are posteriorly related to quadratus lumborum."},{"label":"D","text":"The pancreas is related to the left kidney above the stomach."},{"label":"E","text":"The right kidney is related to the descending colon. 84"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"77e1f0fa098141dbe31e5f832b051d0c363930a0"},{"id":"q-7d0222152600","stem":"30 Which statement about the fascia of the kidney is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The suprarenals lie in the same fascial compart- ment as the kidneys."},{"label":"B","text":"The renal fascia is continuous with fascia over the inferior vena cava and aorta."},{"label":"C","text":"The perinephric fat lies outside the renal fascia."},{"label":"D","text":"The lienorenal ligament is attached to the right kidney. e. The perinephric fat lies deep to the true capsule QUESTIONS of the kidney."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2884c88984e8c709eef83faa38ca179d9022b5d5"},{"id":"q-c23bc9e5ff77","stem":"31 Which of these statements about the pancreas is not correct? ABDOMEN: a. The neck lies in the subcostal plane.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Neck","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"It is supplied by the splenic artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The uncinate process drains via the accessory pancreatic duct."},{"label":"D","text":"It is related to the second part of the duodenum."},{"label":"E","text":"Develops from two buds which arise from the primitive foregut."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d9fe8092d91a","stem":"32 Which of the following does not correctly describe the spleen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Spleen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has a notched superior border."},{"label":"B","text":"Lies under the 9th to 11th ribs."},{"label":"C","text":"Is related directly to the left kidney and the stomach."},{"label":"D","text":"Is completely invested in peritoneum."},{"label":"E","text":"The tail of the pancreas is related to the hilum."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"03fde52b721bbcb229f8adf8960d936fc223a5ff"},{"id":"q-88729bc83aef","stem":"33 Which statement best describes psoas major?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The femoral nerve emerges medial to it."},{"label":"B","text":"The obturator nerve pierces the muscle."},{"label":"C","text":"The genitofemoral nerve emerges lateral to it."},{"label":"D","text":"It is attached distally to the intertrochanteric line."},{"label":"E","text":"The medial arcuate ligament is a condensation of its fascia. 85"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"a1801addba852f65463d7d08b925eadb629a4ce0"},{"id":"q-f7db1488a319","stem":"34 Which statement correctly completes the following sen- tence? The abdominal aorta","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has four lumbar branches."},{"label":"B","text":"Is crossed by the body of the pancreas between the origins of the superior mesenteric artery and inferior mesenteric artery."},{"label":"C","text":"Has the subcostal artery as its first branch."},{"label":"D","text":"Ends at the level of the L5/S1 disc.ABDOMEN: e. Gives three direct branches to the suprarenals."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-076acb905306","stem":"35 Which statement correctly describes the inferior vena cava?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"It commences at the level of L3.QUESTIONS b. It has gastrointestinal tributaries which corre- spond to the equivalent branches of the aorta."},{"label":"C","text":"The second lumbar vein is a tributary."},{"label":"D","text":"The subcostal vein is a tributary."},{"label":"E","text":"The hepatic veins are tributaries."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ed97858f4cf225eb2c070493815a30ac59dff07c"},{"id":"q-63f55b100c9b","stem":"36 Which statement about the lumbar plexus is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is formed by the anterior primary rami of L1–L4."},{"label":"B","text":"The ilioinguinal and iliohypogastric nerves are both derived from L3."},{"label":"C","text":"The femoral and obturator nerves are both derived from the anterior primary rami of L2–L4."},{"label":"D","text":"A branch of the genitofemoral nerve traverses the inguinal canal."},{"label":"E","text":"It is connected to the sacral plexus by the lum- bosacral trunk. 86"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"faafcdbb4a22b587f202b7668be3886c1bae61c9"},{"id":"q-4248b1e5c197","stem":"37 Which statement concerning the abdominal autonomic supply is incorrect? thetic fibres. ABDOMEN:4.38 Which statement best describes the ureter?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Abdomen","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The coeliac ganglia receive fibres from the greater and lesser splanchnic nerves."},{"label":"B","text":"The abdominal organs all derive their sympa- thetic supply from the coeliac ganglia."},{"label":"C","text":"The greater splanchnic nerve contains fibres which innervate the adrenal cortex. d. The sympathetic system contains motor fibres to QUESTIONS the sphincters."},{"label":"E","text":"The pelvic splanchnic nerves contain parasympa-"},{"label":"A","text":"Is narrowest as it crosses the transverse process of L4."},{"label":"B","text":"Is crossed anteriorly by the gonadal vessels."},{"label":"C","text":"Is crossed anteriorly by the root of the mesentery on the left."},{"label":"D","text":"It courses superior to the uterine vessels."},{"label":"E","text":"Has a blood supply from the external iliac artery."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ea4de2255f4f","stem":"39 Which of the following structures does the ureter cross on an abdominal radiograph?","type":"Radiological Interpretation","subject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The bodies of the lumbar vertebrae."},{"label":"B","text":"Ischial tuberosity."},{"label":"C","text":"Sacroiliac joint."},{"label":"D","text":"Pubic tubercle."},{"label":"E","text":"Tragal pointer. 87 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","requires_visual_review","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"b2915c31a60389aba7d7bbd761ad10099a156b10"},{"id":"q-a2ff8182a626","stem":"1 Which of the following statements best describes the PELVIS: bony pelvis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The true pelvis lies between the iliac crests."},{"label":"B","text":"The acetabulum is formed by contributions from all parts of the inominate bone."},{"label":"C","text":"The male pelvic inlet has a more oval shape than in the female."},{"label":"D","text":"The angle between the inferior pubic rami is wider in the male."},{"label":"E","text":"The pelvic outlet is between the symphysis pubis and the sacral tuberosity."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-97f85be7b246","stem":"2 Which of the following statements about the ligaments of the pelvis is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The inguinal ligament passes from the anterior superior iliac spine to the pubic tubercle."},{"label":"B","text":"The sacrospinous ligament is a border of the lesser sciatic foramen."},{"label":"C","text":"The sacrotuberous ligament is a border of the lesser sciatic foramen."},{"label":"D","text":"The lacunar ligament forms the lateral border of the femoral canal."},{"label":"E","text":"The sacrospinous ligament provides an attachment for coccygeus. 109"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"ea15fe8fc05579b25d35492963d7c8538b4d0a09"},{"id":"q-66c4356eb8b1","stem":"3 Which of the following associations of joints and types is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Symphysis pubis Primary cartilaginous"},{"label":"B","text":"Sacroiliac joint Synovial"},{"label":"C","text":"Lumbosacral joint Primary cartilaginous"},{"label":"D","text":"Acetabulofemoral Fibrous"},{"label":"E","text":"Sacrococcygeal FibrousPELVIS:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8f0b7eec30c2c3be7f7123909a42231917273765"},{"id":"q-745a36ff668c","stem":"4 Which of the following structures does not pass through the greater sciatic foramen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Lower Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Piriformis."},{"label":"B","text":"Sciatic nerve.QUESTIONS c. Superior gluteal nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"Inferior gluteal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"Gemellus superior."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6b674426ba43e518239f17bb6df8368e3c844ef8"},{"id":"q-0fc9afd07a78","stem":"5 Which of the following structures passes through the lesser sciatic foramen?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Lower Limb","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The posterior cutaneous nerve of the thigh."},{"label":"B","text":"The pudendal nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"Obturator externus."},{"label":"D","text":"Gemellus superior."},{"label":"E","text":"Gemellus inferior."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Lower Limb · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"81587533cf69a8d1274b6fb973e6496dc04a5b63"},{"id":"q-e46d5d44f532","stem":"6 Which statement most correctly completes the following sentence? Levator ani","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Attaches to the fascia over obturator internus."},{"label":"B","text":"Has fibres which assist continence by pulling the rectum posteriorly."},{"label":"C","text":"Lies inferior to the ischiorectal fossa."},{"label":"D","text":"Is supplied by anterior primary rami of S1 and S2."},{"label":"E","text":"Contracts during defaecation. 110"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-bcd180a65dfa","stem":"7 Which statement about the perineum is the correct one?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Perine","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is divided by a line drawn between the ischial spines."},{"label":"B","text":"The perineal body lies between the anterior and posterior parts of the perineum."},{"label":"C","text":"The perineal membrane lies in the posterior part of the perineum."},{"label":"D","text":"Bartholin’s glands lie deep to the perineal membrane. e. The posterior part of the perineum is bounded lat- QUESTIONS erally by the sacrospinous ligaments."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"5bb7ca9a781e06407f79c70877a0f93806a3dc73"},{"id":"q-270200ce0aad","stem":"8 Which statement about the rectum and its relations is PELVIS: incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"There are two rectal folds on the left."},{"label":"B","text":"The anorectal junction is related to the puborecta- lis muscle."},{"label":"C","text":"The upper 1/3 is entirely invested in peritoneum."},{"label":"D","text":"The pararectal lymph nodes lie in the mesorectum."},{"label":"E","text":"Denonvillier’s fascia lies below the rectovesical pouch."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-adfd95154b04","stem":"9 Which statement best describes the anus and its sphincters?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The anus contains longitudinal and circular muscle."},{"label":"B","text":"The external sphincter is composed of involuntary muscle."},{"label":"C","text":"The external sphincter is continuous with the muscle of the rectum."},{"label":"D","text":"The anorectal ring is formed by puborectalis."},{"label":"E","text":"The anal cushions are found in the left lateral, right posterior and right anterior positions. 111"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"6188dab121c32755311401351bde2dfe494e9b86"},{"id":"q-35c84e1d5dc5","stem":"10 Which statement best describes the bladder? sympathetic fibres.QUESTIONS 5.11 Which statement best describes the pelvic viscera?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Bladder","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The interureteric bar joins the two ureteric orifices."},{"label":"B","text":"The venous drainage follows the course of the arterial supply."},{"label":"C","text":"It has a blood supply principally derived from the external iliac artery.PELVIS: d. It is lined by specialised non-keratinising squa- mous epithelium."},{"label":"E","text":"The sensation of bladder fullness is conveyed by"},{"label":"A","text":"The vas deferens is formed by the union of the ejaculatory ducts and the seminal vesicles."},{"label":"B","text":"The vas deferens runs through the inguinal canal."},{"label":"C","text":"The vas deferens passes anterior to the urethra to enter the bladder."},{"label":"D","text":"The ejaculatory ducts enter the spongy urethra."},{"label":"E","text":"The bulbourethral glands enter the prostatic urethra."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bd49ab4a6c89","stem":"12 Which statement about the prostate is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Prostate","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The urethal crest is found on the posterior wall of the urethra."},{"label":"B","text":"It lies between the bladder and the external ureth- ral sphincter."},{"label":"C","text":"The urethra runs through the posterior part of the gland."},{"label":"D","text":"It may have a true and a false capsule."},{"label":"E","text":"It is supplied by the inferior vesical arteries. 112"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f84884f2d852f90e5a11d6a6674f8c33f240a60a"},{"id":"q-2d99f10189ef","stem":"13 Which statement regarding the male perineum is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Perine","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The root of the penis is attached to the perineal membrane."},{"label":"B","text":"The membranous urethra lies superficial to the perineal membrane."},{"label":"C","text":"Cowper’s glands lie deep to the perineal membrane."},{"label":"D","text":"Colles’ fascia is attached to the perineal membrane. e. The sphincter urethrae contains voluntary muscle. QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b440a96249dca4a10143d6e245cf746cfd26d530"},{"id":"q-8bb510839eff","stem":"14 Which statement best describes the spermatic cord? a. The internal spermatic fascia is derived from the PELVIS: transversus abdominis muscle.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The cremasteric fascia contains muscle fibres derived from external oblique."},{"label":"C","text":"It contains the genital branch of the genitofemo- ral nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"It contains the ilioinguinal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"It contains the testicular vein."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e174a452d592","stem":"15 Which statement best describes the testis and epididymis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The vas deferens arises from the upper pole of the epididymis."},{"label":"B","text":"The appendix testis is attached to the lower pole of the testis."},{"label":"C","text":"The tunica vaginalis lies deep to the tunica albuginea."},{"label":"D","text":"The testis is divided into lobules by septa."},{"label":"E","text":"The dartos muscle lies deep to the cremasteric fascia. 113"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"0027f96e64ae63d80e89aec0185956c09aed1692"},{"id":"q-d5590432fb59","stem":"16 Which statement concerning the penis is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The corpora cavernosa are ensheathed by the tunica albuginea."},{"label":"B","text":"The penile urethra runs within the corpus spongiosum."},{"label":"C","text":"There are two deep penile arteries."},{"label":"D","text":"Erection is under sympathetic control.PELVIS: e. Bulbospongiosus is important in micturition."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4b99e7e809237485635f5d413eba99b173f9327e"},{"id":"q-bf588c4c0041","stem":"17 Which statement about the uterus and fallopian tubes is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The fundus lies posterior to the entrance of theQUESTIONS fallopian tubes into the uterus."},{"label":"B","text":"The cornu is the point of junction of the body of the uterus and the vagina."},{"label":"C","text":"The ampulla of the fallopian tubes bare fimbrae."},{"label":"D","text":"The fallopian tubes contain smooth muscle."},{"label":"E","text":"The upper part drains lymph to the external iliac nodes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"c41b3366ae655dfa53f1520dfd184fc0accb972c"},{"id":"q-a376bc574b82","stem":"18 Which of the following statements about the uterus is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The uterus is retroverted in 1/5 of nulliparous females."},{"label":"B","text":"The uterine artery courses down the lateral wall of the uterus."},{"label":"C","text":"The cervix is attached to the bladder."},{"label":"D","text":"Develops from the paramesonephric ducts."},{"label":"E","text":"The cardinal ligament is traversed by the ureter."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"a101f1fb99741672d2682fbbc13963b02a668da6"},{"id":"q-f74fda1cf9ad","stem":"19 Which statement concerning the ovary is the correct one?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ovarian ligament contains the ovarian vessels."},{"label":"B","text":"The right ovarian vein drains into the right renal vein."},{"label":"C","text":"The suspensory ligament of the ovary is attached to the sidewall of the pelvis."},{"label":"D","text":"Lymphatics drain to the internal iliac nodes."},{"label":"E","text":"It is attached to the anterior aspect of the broad ligament. 114"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"691b7a29fa4b71570bdeab32acef0a8eddc0b5d1"},{"id":"q-445700e2e5a7","stem":"20 Which structure is not contained within, or attached to, the broad ligament?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The suspensory ligament of the ovary."},{"label":"B","text":"The round ligament."},{"label":"C","text":"The uterine artery."},{"label":"D","text":"The fallopian tube."},{"label":"E","text":"The ovarian ligament."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e99d0dbb5561772c324aaf25e081451cef1ff56b"},{"id":"q-b2967922763c","stem":"21 Which statement best describes the cervix and vagina? a. The anterior part of the cervix is covered with QUESTIONS peritoneum.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Abdomen","topicOriginal":"Abdomen","subtopic":"Peritone","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"The vagina is covered with peritoneum anteriorly. c. The ureter is a close relation of the cervix. PELVIS:"},{"label":"D","text":"The entire vagina is supplied with sensory fibres by the pudendal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The majority of the lymph from the vagina drains to the superficial inguinal nodes."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Abdomen","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b0819f08306c","stem":"22 Which statement about the pelvic vasculature is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The common iliac artery divides over the sacro- iliac joint."},{"label":"B","text":"The external iliac artery divides into anterior and posterior branches."},{"label":"C","text":"The ovarian artery is a branch of the internal iliac artery."},{"label":"D","text":"The inferior epigastric artery is a branch of the internal iliac artery."},{"label":"E","text":"The obturator artery is a branch of the external iliac artery. 115"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"ebcac2c81d049d8b4d70b0e961f7bacf75034a15"},{"id":"q-31fbbb2625c3","stem":"23 Which statement regarding the nerve supply of mictu- rition is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Contraction of the detrusor muscle is initiated by fibres from the inferior hypogastric plexus."},{"label":"B","text":"The sphincter urethrae is innervated by the para- sympathetic system."},{"label":"C","text":"The internal urethral sphincter is parasympathet-PELVIS: ically innervated."},{"label":"D","text":"Pubovaginalis helps to maintain continence in the female."},{"label":"E","text":"Following a lumbar cord transection, bladder voiding is impossible.QUESTIONS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2ee6c69f8efdae3b94c685b7b461e3c5b347040b"},{"id":"q-2fea7034a3b3","stem":"24 Which statement does not correctly complete this sen- tence? The pudendal nerve","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Enters the pelvis through the lesser sciatic foramen."},{"label":"B","text":"Runs in a canal formed by the obturator internus fascia."},{"label":"C","text":"Has a dorsal branch which is sensory to the penis."},{"label":"D","text":"Has a perineal branch which is sensory to the clitoris."},{"label":"E","text":"Gives motor fibres to the muscles of the urogeni- tal diaphragm. 116 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c0e46b33eb78","stem":"1 Which statement about the neurocranium is correct? AND","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The bregma is the adult remnant of the posterior fontanelle. b. The metopic suture usually disappears in the first HEAD year of life."},{"label":"C","text":"The anterior fontanelle is not palpable past 1 year of age."},{"label":"D","text":"Six bones make up the adult neurocranium."},{"label":"E","text":"The pterion represents the thinnest part of the lat- eral skull."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c6ef3d3d31f2","stem":"2 Which statement regarding the foramina of the skull is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Head and Neck","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The inferior ophthalmic vein passes through the inferior orbital fissure."},{"label":"B","text":"The foramen spinosum connects the middle cra- nial fossa with the infratemporal fossa."},{"label":"C","text":"The foramen ovale transmits the maxillary div- ision of the trigeminal nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"The optic nerve enters the skull in the anterior cranial fossa."},{"label":"E","text":"The hypoglossal nerve exits the skull via the jugu- lar foramen. 129"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f0fc6a8f0ecc92708c4552983512f2ab3a0e8675"},{"id":"q-247a61d28324","stem":"3 Which statement best describes the cranial fossae?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Cranial","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The middle cranial fossa contains the cribriform plate."},{"label":"B","text":"The anterior cranial fossa contains the pituitary gland.HEAD"},{"label":"C","text":"The middle cranial fossa is floored by the sphenoid and temporal bones.AND"},{"label":"D","text":"The internal acoustic meatus lies in the middle cranial fossa.NECK: e. The occipital lobe lies in the posterior cranial fossa."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"1ee97c58e9a8b337031f4e40e17656aa742601b1"},{"id":"q-2428bffb9309","stem":"4 Which statement concerning the development of the face is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Face","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Frontonasal process forms the nose.QUESTIONS b. Frontonasal process forms the premaxilla."},{"label":"C","text":"Maxillary processes fuse in the midline."},{"label":"D","text":"Maxillary processes forms the entire palate."},{"label":"E","text":"Mandibular processes fuse in the midline."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"88d87bfe057ad877b29e2b7f04f21788fde19a7f"},{"id":"q-c8ad4e69326b","stem":"5 Which statement best describes the branchial arches and their derivatives?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Five branchial arches form in human embryos."},{"label":"B","text":"The ossicles of the middle ear are all skeletal deriva- tives of the first arch."},{"label":"C","text":"The muscles of facial expression are derived from the second arch."},{"label":"D","text":"The nerve of the third arch is the vagus."},{"label":"E","text":"The artery of the first arch forms part of the internal carotid artery. 130"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"0adf20ad611dbab5037c40a3431dacbd6eb59f1f"},{"id":"q-7536d4d82b32","stem":"6 Which of the following statements about the eye are incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Ophthalmology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Aqueous humour is drained via the canal of Schlemm."},{"label":"B","text":"Greatest visual acuity is found at the macula densa."},{"label":"C","text":"The optic nerve is invested by all three meningeal layers. d. The central artery of the retina is an end artery. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"Parasympathetic fibres from the oculomotor nerve innervate the lacrimal gland. NECK:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Ophthalmology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"acb29e129973981e371b7d34b7359a3733aa4111"},{"id":"q-44a3e16cc752","stem":"7 Which statement best describes the muscles of the eye? AND a. The superior and inferior obliques arise from the tendinous ring.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"B","text":"The superior oblique is innervated by the oculo- HEAD motor nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"Sphincter pupillae is innervated by sympathetic nerves."},{"label":"D","text":"Oculomotor nerve paralysis causes a complete ptosis."},{"label":"E","text":"Closure of the eye is controlled by the facial nerve."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3aa31d4ec5d9","stem":"8 Which statement best describes the middle ear?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The medial wall is formed by the tympanic membrane."},{"label":"B","text":"The epitympanic recess contains the incus and head of the stapes."},{"label":"C","text":"The internal jugular vein is related to its roof."},{"label":"D","text":"It communicates with the mastoid air cells inferiorly."},{"label":"E","text":"The Eustachian tube runs from the anterior wall of the middle ear to the oropharynx. 131"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"fadcbd596d4562d29634af6002c75ca77cb6ecd0"},{"id":"q-b6dd24bd9aa8","stem":"9 Which statement about the nasal septum is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Nasal","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is formed by the septal cartilage posteriorly."},{"label":"B","text":"Is formed by the perpendicular plate of the eth- moid postero-inferiorly."},{"label":"C","text":"Is lined by mucoperiosteum throughout.HEAD"},{"label":"D","text":"Little’s area overlies the vomer."},{"label":"E","text":"The sphenopalatine artery courses over the septum.AND"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"33f9f215e5bec1b2a690d9d17c899750d04898dc"},{"id":"q-00ed35eaeecf","stem":"10 Consider the lateral wall of the nasal cavity, which state-NECK: ment describes it the best?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Nasal","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is formed principally by the ethmoid bone."},{"label":"B","text":"The nasal bone forms the anterior part of the lat- eral wall."},{"label":"C","text":"The inferior concha is part of the maxilla.QUESTIONS d. The superior concha is part of the maxilla."},{"label":"E","text":"The superior meatus lies above the superior turbinate."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1ff3ff0d1ffd","stem":"11 Which statement about the maxillary sinus is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is lined by respiratory mucous membrane."},{"label":"B","text":"Forms the floor of the orbit via its roof."},{"label":"C","text":"Is drained from its most dependent part."},{"label":"D","text":"Drains into the middle meatus."},{"label":"E","text":"Is supplied by branches of the maxillary nerve."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"583b02204caff799b2804b84374002e4f4267909"},{"id":"q-16192a8a9098","stem":"12 Which statement describing the ethmoid sinuses is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"They lie between the orbit and the nasal cavity."},{"label":"B","text":"They form six distinct cavities."},{"label":"C","text":"The anterior ethmoidal air cells drain into the middle meatus."},{"label":"D","text":"The posterior ethmoidal air cells drain into the superior meatus."},{"label":"E","text":"Are supplied by branches from both the oph- thalmic and maxillary branches of the trigeminal nerve. 132"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"d2d2b717b3bffa030a13312ff5362ccdc77d4360"},{"id":"q-ecd20abf0383","stem":"13 Which statement concerning the paranasal sinuses is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Nasal","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The sphenoid sinuses are medial to the cavernous sinus."},{"label":"B","text":"The sphenoid sinuses open into the nasal cavity behind the superior concha."},{"label":"C","text":"The frontal sinuses are not present at birth. d. The frontal sinus is related to the orbit. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"E","text":"The frontal sinus drains into the superior meatus. NECK:6.14 Which of the following statements does not correctly describe the oral cavity? AND a. Taste sensation for the posterior 1/3 of the tongue is supplied by the glossopharyngeal nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"The sensory innervation for the anterior 2/3 of HEAD the tongue is provided by the trigeminal nerve."},{"label":"C","text":"The four extrinsic muscles of the tongue are sup- plied by the hypoglossal nerve."},{"label":"D","text":"Lesions of the hypoglossal nerve cause ipsilateral deviation of the tongue on protrusion."},{"label":"E","text":"The teeth are innervated by divisions of the trigeminal nerve."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"6cfdd83723d2a007c94e67f65e1bd067c2b9bc34"},{"id":"q-a877addef96f","stem":"15 Which statement best describes the anatomy of the tongue?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The anterior 1/3 is separated from the posterior 2/3 by the sulcus terminalis."},{"label":"B","text":"Receives its blood supply from a direct branch of the external carotid artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The posterior 1/3 drains lymph to the lower part of the deep cervical chain of lymph nodes."},{"label":"D","text":"Common sensation to the anterior 2/3 of the tongue is derived from the facial nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The intrinsic muscles of the tongue are all inner- vated by the facial nerve. 133"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"e1a87c9e53c8e0f3653b71cfbd1fa6f0da1a13fc"},{"id":"q-5e677573d983","stem":"16 Which of the following is not true of the palatine tonsil?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has the palatopharyngeal arch as a direct anterior relation."},{"label":"B","text":"Is separated by its capsule from the superior con- strictor of the pharynx.HEAD"},{"label":"C","text":"Derives its blood supply principally from the facial artery.AND"},{"label":"D","text":"Has the paratonsillar vein as a lateral relation."},{"label":"E","text":"Drains its lymph to nodes along the internal jugu-NECK: lar vein."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"71f7f460092ba8d295f26abe5bc66110a2b288b1"},{"id":"q-3cd034f3ea1b","stem":"17 Which statement incorrectly describes the muscles of mastication?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Dislocation of the temporomandibular joint usu-QUESTIONS ally occurs anteriorly."},{"label":"B","text":"The medial pterygoid takes origin from the lateral pterygoid plate."},{"label":"C","text":"Of the muscles of mastication only the lateral pterygoid is involved in protracting the mandible."},{"label":"D","text":"All the muscles of mastication are innervated by the maxillary division of the trigeminal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"All of the muscles of mastication are supplied by branches of the maxillary artery."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"e76ffc4f3d6028313a194124b6d1db78cc5833e5"},{"id":"q-83918c127241","stem":"18 Which statement regarding the parotid gland is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Parotid","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The parotid duct opens into the oral cavity oppos- ite the second lower molar tooth."},{"label":"B","text":"The parotid duct runs deep to masseter through- out its course."},{"label":"C","text":"Preganglionic parasympathetic fibres innervat- ing the parotid originate in the superior salivary nucleus."},{"label":"D","text":"Postganglionic parasympathetic fibres originate in the submandibular ganglion."},{"label":"E","text":"Sympathetic innervation to the parotid follows the external carotid artery. 134"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"14e2014bab1e0d635f4ba9c9dc51b13721f1e5fe"},{"id":"q-365b1212b08d","stem":"19 Which of the following statements best describes the salivary glands?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The stylomandibular ligament separates the sub- mandibular and sublingual glands."},{"label":"B","text":"The parotid duct is also known as Wharton’s duct."},{"label":"C","text":"Stensen’s duct empties alongside the frenulum of the tongue. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"D","text":"Postganglionic parasympathetic fibres to the sub- mandibular gland are transmitted via the chorda NECK: tympani nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The submandibular gland is related to the poster- AND ior border of mylohyoid."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"4bcc41ab14ab58fad570d5ffc4e38e412b3ec4b3"},{"id":"q-bc7d03e08151","stem":"20 Which statement about the surface anatomy of the neck HEAD is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Face","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The hard palate lies at the same level as the atlas."},{"label":"B","text":"The hyoid lies at the level of C4."},{"label":"C","text":"The cricoid lies at the level of C5."},{"label":"D","text":"The oesophagus commences at the level of C7."},{"label":"E","text":"The carotid tubercle lies at the level of C3."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c66e203c3b21","stem":"21 Which of the following statements about the anterior triangle of the neck is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Neck","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lies between the midline, the mandible and the anterior border of sternocleidomastoid."},{"label":"B","text":"Is further divided by the digastric and omohyoid muscles."},{"label":"C","text":"Contains the submandibular gland."},{"label":"D","text":"Contains the external jugular vein."},{"label":"E","text":"Contains the carotid sheath. 135"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"da0804ec51504dddaad27573f43c51c4950a98c3"},{"id":"q-12c0e8902cfc","stem":"22 Which of these statements about the posterior triangle of the neck is incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Neck","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is bounded by the sternocleidomastoid, trapez- ius and the middle third of the clavicle."},{"label":"B","text":"It contains the spinal accessory nerve.HEAD"},{"label":"C","text":"The spinal accessory nerve can be identified at the posterior border of sternocleidomastoid.AND"},{"label":"D","text":"It is floored by prevertebral fascia."},{"label":"E","text":"It contains the first part of the subclavian artery.NECK:"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"354cf31ed79734ae51c8c311d81081c2980c7697"},{"id":"q-4168e4fe2caa","stem":"23 Which statement about the fascial planes of the neck is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Neck","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The investing layer of fascia completely sur- rounds the neck.QUESTIONS b. The investing layer of fascia contributes to the capsule of the parotid gland."},{"label":"C","text":"The prevertebral fascia is continuous with the axillary sheath."},{"label":"D","text":"The pretracheal fascia has two layers."},{"label":"E","text":"The prevertebral fascia merges with the pericardium."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"085426cb8d625293d465edff49b97b48013f97ed"},{"id":"q-1c4183098e67","stem":"24 Which statement concerning the muscles of the neck is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Neck","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The tendon of omohyoid overlies the internal jugular vein."},{"label":"B","text":"The suprahyoid muscles are supplied by the ansa cervicalis."},{"label":"C","text":"Sternothyroid lies superficial to sternohyoid."},{"label":"D","text":"Stylohyoid is supplied by the glossopharyngeal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"Mylohyoid is supplied by the facial nerve. 136"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"96bd5af6445cb837c802cc37228d3ca216ea66c1"},{"id":"q-6fe06f958268","stem":"25 Which of the following statements describing the phar- ynx is incorrect? incorrect?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The nasopharynx derives its sensory innervation from the trigeminal nerve."},{"label":"B","text":"The glossopharyngeal nerve passes between the superior and middle constrictors."},{"label":"C","text":"It is lined by stratified squamous epithelium throughout. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"D","text":"The weakest part of the muscular wall is at the level of the inferior constrictor. NECK: e. It ends at the level of C6. AND6.26 Which of the following statements about the larynx is"},{"label":"A","text":"The laryngeal inlet opens into the laryngopharynx. HEAD"},{"label":"B","text":"The vestibule of the larynx lies between the ves- tibular fold and the vocal fold."},{"label":"C","text":"The narrowest part of the larynx in an adult is at the level of the vocal folds."},{"label":"D","text":"The cricothyroid membrane forms the vocal ligament."},{"label":"E","text":"The infraglottic portion is supplied by the inferior thyroid artery."}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a8adc2ad7188","stem":"27 Which statement, concerning the larynx is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The supraglottic part of the larynx drains to the upper deep cervical nodes."},{"label":"B","text":"The vocal folds drain to the inferior deep cervical nodes."},{"label":"C","text":"The cricothyroid is the only muscle to abduct the vocal cords."},{"label":"D","text":"The posterior cricoarytenoid is supplied by the superior laryngeal nerve."},{"label":"E","text":"The vocal folds are cushioned by a layer of submucosa. 137"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2ea64af99230be23806f5abe9a9e3724f398b9d2"},{"id":"q-efab6ca579be","stem":"28 Which statement about the blood supply of the thyroid is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inferior thyroid artery is a branch of the external carotid artery."},{"label":"B","text":"Inferior thyroid artery normally supplies theHEAD superior and inferior parathyroids."},{"label":"C","text":"Thyroidea ima usually arises from the arch of theAND aorta."},{"label":"D","text":"Middle thyroid vein drains into the brachio-NECK: cephalic vein."},{"label":"E","text":"External laryngeal nerve is closely related to the inferior thyroid vessels."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"2b52742b14c5cb15123977058dac37a8a22e3d1d"},{"id":"q-6b77e0a6bc5d","stem":"29 Which statement regarding the development of the thy-QUESTIONS roid and parathyroids is not correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The thyroid is in its approximate adult position at birth."},{"label":"B","text":"The foramen caecum is an embryological rem- nant of the thyroid’s development."},{"label":"C","text":"Levator glandulae thyroidae is an embryological remnant of the thyroid’s development."},{"label":"D","text":"The inferior parathyroid glands develop from the 3rd branchial arch."},{"label":"E","text":"The superior parathyroids are more variable in position than the inferior parathyroids."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0e626b8e0e60","stem":"30 Which statement concerning the parathyroid glands is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Head and Neck","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Four glands are present in 50% of subjects."},{"label":"B","text":"The superior parathyroid lies above the superior thyroid artery."},{"label":"C","text":"The parathyroids have a combined weight of 1g."},{"label":"D","text":"Oxyphil cells secrete parathyroid hormone."},{"label":"E","text":"The superior parathyroid lies within the pretra- cheal fascia. 138"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"159e452fa5b958b5502218bc056a0481542434af"},{"id":"q-9287578187db","stem":"31 Which statement best describes the external carotid artery and its branches?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Histology and Tissues","topicOriginal":"Histology and Tissues","subtopic":"Artery","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The anterior part of the scalp is supplied by the facial branch of the external carotid."},{"label":"B","text":"The maxillary artery is divided into three parts by the lateral pterygoid muscle."},{"label":"C","text":"The facial artery is easily palpable at the anterior border of masseter. QUESTIONS"},{"label":"D","text":"The lingual artery gives the superior laryngeal artery as a branch. NECK: e. The middle meningeal artery is a branch of the facial artery. AND"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Histology and Tissues","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"81777ff14cbf63b078779ac78da52319899b4ad3"},{"id":"q-80b81958be12","stem":"32 Which statement regarding the lymphatic drainage of the head and neck is incorrect? HEAD","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Head","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"All the lymph drainage from the face enters the deep cervical nodes."},{"label":"B","text":"The left deep cervical nodes drain into the thor- acic duct."},{"label":"C","text":"The right lymphatic duct drains into the junction between the right internal jugular and brachio- cephalic veins."},{"label":"D","text":"The superficial cervical nodes lie along the exter- nal jugular vein."},{"label":"E","text":"The jugulo-omohyoid node is easily palpable when enlarged. 139 ANSWERS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-51e16575cc5a","stem":"13ANSWERS e. The frontal sinus drains into the middle meatus. Explanations","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The sphenoid sinuses lie in the body of the sphenoid bone. They are related superiorly to the pituitary fossa and 146 middle cranial fossa, and laterally to the cavernous sinus and internal carotid artery."},{"label":"B","text":"The sphenoid sinuses open into the spheno-ethmoidal recess which lies behind the superior concha."},{"label":"C","text":"The frontal sinuses start to develop in the second year of life. They are the only paranasal sinuses not present at birth."},{"label":"D","text":"The frontal sinus is related to the orbit and to the anterior cranial fossa. Infection of the frontal sinus may therefore lead to the formation of a frontal lobe abscess."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-ac45fef25e4f","stem":"which articulates with the clavicle. The spine of the scap","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2ed9c62fe5d7","stem":"which are the attachment sites of supraspinatus, infraspina","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ae0bf629fb96","stem":"which empty at the nipple via the lactiferous sinus.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0c2c393ef349","stem":"where it is superficial, easily palpable and prone to injury. LIMB","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options