ns":[]},{"id":"q-030f25e2bd16","stem":"TUMAINI UNIVERSITY KILIMANJARO CHRISTIAN MEDICAL COLLEGE UNIVERSITY EXAMINATIONS CODE : ANA 104 SUBJECT : ANATOMY & HISTOLOGY PAPER I PROGRAMME : MD I DATE : 01/08/2008 TIME : 8.30 - 11:30 AM INSTRUCTIONS TO CANDIDATES 1. Write your examination Code Number on each examination sheet and never your name. 2. Write answer on the examination sheets provided for Multiple choice Questions and answer the rest on the spaces provided. 3. This is a THREE-HOUR paper consisting of EIGHTEEN printed pages with FIVE sections. Section I : Multiple-Choice Questions Section II : Filling the gaps Section III : True or False Section IV : Matching items Section V : Labelling diagrams 4. Read each question carefully. 5. Attempt all questions. SECTION I - MULTIPLE CHOICE QUESTION (@1mark) The Dura fold that divides the two cerebellar hemispheres is called? Falx cerebri","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy","topicOriginal":"Neuroanatomy","subtopic":"Cerebell","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Falx cerebelli Transverse sinus Tentorium cerebelli Regarding cells of the nervous system;"},{"label":"B","text":"Pyramidal neurons are pseudopolar Schimid - Lantermann clefts occurs in myelin"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d51b25415f4e","stem":"Nodes of Ranvier facilitate salutatory conductions Oligodendrocytes myelinate nerve fibers in the CNS Which cell is a macrophage found in the central nervous system?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":