atus is located between the fused vertebrae. sacral cornua and inferior to the 4th sacral spinous process or median sacral crest.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Anesthesiology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Anesthesiology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-bf3f67e40473","stem":"Which of the following statements about kyphosis is true? 37. Which of the following is NOT a vertebral problem? (A) Kyphosis may result from developmental anomalies as well as from osteoporosis. (A) sacralization of L5 (B) The vertebral column curves anteriorly. (B) lumbarization of S1 (C) Kyphosis results in an increase in the lat- (C) lumbarization of T12 eral diameter of the thorax. (D) lumbar spinal stenosis (D) Women may develop a temporary kypho- (E) hemisacralization of L5 sis during pregnancy. (E) It is also known as “swayback” or 38. Which of the following statements is true? “hollow back.” (A) In spina bifida cystica, the laminae of L5 and possibly S1 do not fuse properly.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem",