ment of blood pressure. Which of the following statements about this unit is true?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is part of the Australian Metric System but not part of the SI system."},{"label":"B","text":"It is part of the SI system but not part of the Australian Metric System."},{"label":"C","text":"It belongs to both the SI system and the Australian Metric System."},{"label":"D","text":"It does not belong to either the SI system or the Australian Metric System."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"de3727eb34d16a11e100165db9e484c0b0b5691b"},{"id":"q-7b3fc0032362","stem":"The chemical formula C6H12O6 contains much information. However, what information is NOT provided by the formula?","type":"Calculation","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the number of atoms in a molecule"},{"label":"B","text":"the name of the substance © Springer Science+Business Media Singapore 2016 43 M. Caon, Examination Questions and Answers in Basic Anatomy and Physiology, DOI 10.1007/978-981-10-2332-3_4 44 4 Chemistry for Physiology"},{"label":"C","text":"the elements that make up the substance"},{"label":"D","text":"whether the substance is covalent or ionic"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"e3d7463dad86dcfd4aa53a8fbc6e422a6914c5d1"},{"id":"q-d8feb78ff453","stem":"Which of the particles listed below is the smallest?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"an atom"},{"label":"B","text":"a proton"},{"label":"C","text":"an ion"},{"label":"D","text":"a molecule"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"provisional_independently_reasoned","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"]},{"id":"q-cc64bd257f17","stem":"The chemical name for sodium is which of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Na"},{"label":"B","text":"So"},{"label":"C","text":"K"},{"label":"D","text":"Si"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{"sourceStem":"The chemical name for sodium is which of the following?","sourceOptions":[{"label":"A","text":"Na"},{"label":"B","text":"So"},{"label":"C","text":"K"},{"label":"D","text":"Si Answer is A: Na is short for Natrium which is the Latin name for sodium."}]}},{"id":"q-4b4720c8270e","stem":"A molecular compound may be defined by which of the following?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"atoms from non-metal elements covalently bonded."},{"label":"B","text":"atoms from metal elements covalently bonded"},{"label":"C","text":"atoms from metal elements and non-metal elements covalently bonded"},{"label":"D","text":"atoms from non-metal elements ironically bonded"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"]},{"id":"q-ae79367bc0b8","stem":"Many drugs are neutralised to form salts and administered in this form. What is the main advantage of administering the salt form of the drug? It is usually","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"less toxic"},{"label":"B","text":"more soluble in water"},{"label":"C","text":"more pleasant to taste"},{"label":"D","text":"more soluble in lipid"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{"sourceStem":"Many drugs are neutralised to form salts and administered in this form. What is the main advantage of administering the salt form of the drug? It is usually","sourceOptions":[{"label":"A","text":"less toxic"},{"label":"B","text":"more soluble in water"},{"label":"C","text":"more pleasant to taste"},{"label":"D","text":"more soluble in lipid Answer is B: salts, having particles that are electrically charged, are more likely to be soluble in water."}],"operations":["trailing_answer_leakage_removed"]}},{"id":"q-fcbcfbbefb6c","stem":"One of the following is INCORRECT. Which one?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"metal atoms will form compounds with non-metal atoms."},{"label":"B","text":"metal atoms will form compounds with metal atoms."},{"label":"C","text":"non-metal atoms will form compounds with non-metal atoms."},{"label":"D","text":"metal atoms will not form compounds with metal atoms."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"7daef4b2129576a98dba3b366db1332357c9b1b8"},{"id":"q-5325e855e8ea","stem":"Choose the correct statement about hydrogen bonds. They","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"are stronger than covalent bonds."},{"label":"B","text":"act between the H in one –OH or –NH group, and the O or N in another."},{"label":"C","text":"operate within molecules."},{"label":"D","text":"act between the H in one –OH or –NH group, and the H in another."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"]},{"id":"q-58ae0fbbf8d4","stem":"Given that the atomic mass of nitrogen is 14 and of hydrogen is 1, what is the mass in grams of one mole of ammonia (NH3)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"15"},{"label":"B","text":"16"},{"label":"C","text":"17"},{"label":"D","text":"18"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_reasoning_unverified_sources","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"]},{"id":"q-c78a6364bcbb","stem":"Choose the ending that will correctly complete the sentence: When atoms of a metal element and atoms of a non-metal element react, the result is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"a covalent compound consisting of molecules"},{"label":"B","text":"a covalent compound consisting of ions"},{"label":"C","text":"an ionic compound consisting of ions in a lattice"},{"label":"D","tex